"""Ordinary talk: the things people say that call for no best-friend move at all. Their day, a chore, a how-to, a big
life decision, a word to Luma about its settings, a worry, a name dropped in passing.

The packs teach the small model what a take or a spat sounds like. This teaches it the other side, which matters more:
most of what anyone says is none of those, and a "pick a side" line on "should i quit my job" would be a bad friend.

Same format as a pack (blanks in braces), with no move. A blank in BORROWED is filled from a pack, so the same names
turn up here with no ask around them: "we watched {movie} last night" is not a take on the movie."""

BORROWED = {"game": ("games", "game"), "artist": ("music", "artist"), "movie": ("screen", "movie"), "show": ("screen", "show"),
            "team": ("sports", "team"), "celeb": ("drama", "celeb")}

